# XCU 1.2 Utility Limits
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The minimum values of the utility limits are observed through getconf and
# the utilities the limits apply to.

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/Utility Limit Minimum Values
class      required
since      1992
says       getconf reports, for each of the symbolic utility limits BC_BASE_MAX,
           BC_DIM_MAX, BC_SCALE_MAX, BC_STRING_MAX, COLL_WEIGHTS_MAX,
           EXPR_NEST_MAX, LINE_MAX and RE_DUP_MAX, an integer that is at least
           the stated minimum.
test       t/001-getconf-minimums.sh

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/{LINE_MAX}
class      required
since      1992
says       Text utilities process input lines of 2047 bytes plus the newline
           unchanged: cat, sort, sed, awk, cut, head, tail, uniq, grep, tee,
           paste and wc.
timeout    60
test       t/002-line-max-lines.sh

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/{RE_DUP_MAX}
class      required
since      1992
says       An interval expression may repeat 255 times in a BRE and an ERE:
           a{255} matches a line of exactly 255 a characters and does not match
           254.
test       t/003-re-dup-max.sh

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/{EXPR_NEST_MAX}
class      required
since      1992
says       expr evaluates an expression nested in 32 levels of parentheses.
test       t/004-expr-nesting.sh

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/{BC_BASE_MAX}
class      required
since      1992
says       bc supports an output base of 99, a scale of 99, an array index of
           2047 and a string constant of 1000 bytes.
test       t/005-bc-limits.sh

assertion  XCU.1.2-utility-limits.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.2/All numeric limits defined by the System Interfaces volume
class      required
since      1992
says       The limits of the System Interfaces apply to utilities: getconf
           reports PATH_MAX of at least 256 and NAME_MAX of at least 14, and
           pathchk accepts a path of 239 bytes made of components of 14 bytes.
test       t/006-path-limits.sh
